    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        40,
        400
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        300
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "How to use\n\n1. Pick your checkpoint in Load Checkpoint.\n2. While exploring prompts, select the hires-pass nodes (ImageScaleBy through Save Image) and press Ctrl+B to bypass them. You then only get the fast base preview.\n3. When you like an image, set the base KSampler seed to fixed, un-bypass the hires nodes (Ctrl+B again) and run once more.\n\nHires pass: denoise 0.35 to 0.45 adds detail. Higher values start changing the picture.\nIf the hires pass runs out of memory, lower scale_by to 1.3 or start ComfyUI with --lowvram.\n\nAnime Post FX: set any effect to 0 to turn it off.\n\nFace detailer: finds the face, redraws it at high resolution (guide_size 768) and pastes it back. This is what fixes small or broken eyes in full-body shots. denoise 0.35 to 0.5: higher changes the face more. To skip it, select the FaceDetailer node and press Ctrl+B.\n\nHand detailer: runs after the face detailer and redraws each detected hand (guide_size 512, denoise 0.4), which fixes most broken fingers. Adds about 40 s. To skip it, select the HandDetailer node and press Ctrl+B."
      ]
    },
